  "description": "Cross-platform filename and path validation and sanitization for .NET: the pathvalidate for .NET. Turn any user-supplied name into a safe filename that will not break, overwrite, or open a path-traversal hole. Handles the traps hand-rolled Path.GetInvalidFileNameChars() loops miss: Windows reserved device names (CON, PRN, AUX, NUL, COM1-9, LPT1-9, including with any extension and case-insensitively), trailing dots and spaces (which Windows silently strips), UTF-8 byte length limits (not just character counts), control characters, DEL, path separators, and the reserved characters that differ per platform. Per-platform profiles (Windows, POSIX, Universal, Auto), extension-preserving length truncation, configurable replacement, reserved-name policy, and a detailed Validate API with per-error reasons and positions. Sanitize never throws on the input name and its output is guaranteed to pass Validate for the same profile. Includes a full-path sanitizer that neutralizes traversal and rejoins with the platform separator. Zero external dependencies.",
  "id": "SafeName",
